        "t1": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABKQkLsw",
            "number": 1615,
            "title": "fix(response): keep `iterable` streaming past skipped values",
            "body": "`iterable()` drops `undefined` values and values the serializer returns `undefined` for, but the `pull()` call that drops one resolves without enqueuing anything. `ReadableStream` only calls `pull()` again if another read arrived while it was running, so a pending read can be left unanswered and the response never finishes. Consecutive or trailing skips can trigger it on both web and node:\n\n```ts\niterable([\"a\", undefined, \"b\", undefined]); // hangs, expected \"ab\"\niterable([\"a\", \"skip\", \"skip\", \"b\"], { serializer }); // serializer returns undefined for \"skip\"; hangs, expected \"ab\"\n```\n\n`pull()` now keeps reading until it enqueues a chunk or the iterator is done. Values that serialize to a chunk are handled as before.\n\n- Ran: `pnpm vitest run test/iterable.test.ts`: both new tests time out on `main` in web and node (4 failed, 38 passed) and pass with the fix (42 passed).\n- Ran: `pnpm vitest run --coverage`: 73 files, 3134 passed, 51 skipped.\n- Checked: `pnpm typecheck`, `oxlint .` and `pnpm build` pass; `oxfmt --check` is clean on the changed files.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Response streams continue past values that produce no output, allowing later values to be delivered.\n  * Values that cannot be serialized are omitted without interrupting the remaining stream.\n  * Streams close when iteration finishes, including when the final value has no serializable output.\n  * After cancellation, streams stop reading additional values and do not serialize values that arrive afterward.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
            "state": "OPEN",
            "isDraft": false,
